    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d79">

                <pb facs="0210" n="106" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg106"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">130 Howe, Audrey Marie</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at Winnipeg
                        (Heintzleman)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-02-09">February 9,
                        1933</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>With reference to the registration application which was executed in your office
                    on July 20, 1932, by Miss Audrey Marie Howe and the Department’s instruction of
                    July 25, 1932,<anchor n="67" xml:id="d79-f1"/> approving the registration you
                    are informed that the case of Miss Howe has been receiving further consideration
                    by the Department and it has been ascertained that the oath of allegiance taken
                    by her in connection with her position as a teacher in the schools of the
                    Province of Alberta was in no way qualified. Accordingly, the Department is of
                    the opinion that the oath taken is such an oath as is contemplated by the first
                    paragraph of Section 2 of the Act of March 2, 1907, and that the taking of such
                    an oath resulted in the loss of American citizenship by Miss Howe. You will,
                    therefore, cancel the record of her registration in your office.</p>
                <closer>[File copy not signed]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
